        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Hong Kong</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1841 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">People lived in the area for tens of thousands of years; as a city it grew from the British colony on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong-island">Hong Kong Island</a>, occupied on 26 January 1841 and formally ceded to the United Kingdom in the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanking</a> in 1842.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s southern coast, on the eastern side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pearl-river">Pearl River</a> estuary, 60 km east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a> and south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shenzhen">Shenzhen</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong-island">Hong Kong Island</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kowloon">Kowloon</a> Peninsula, the New Territories and over 200 other islands.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A British colony from 1841 to 1997; a free port and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a>; the Japanese occupation of 1941 to 1945; refugees from mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>; industrialisation in the 1950s; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-british-joint-declaration">Sino-British Joint Declaration</a> of 1984; the handover of 1997</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Hong Kong is a special administrative region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, with about 7.5 million residents, governed under the principle of one country, two systems.</span></div>
